60,3,1,talk,Rin,,"@Everyone, I vote for B! Moving it means no one gets stuck with the stink forever. I don't want a smelly box!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Midori,,"@Rin, I understand your worry. But the subsidy only covers forty percent, capped at ninety thousand. The shelters cost two hundred forty-eight thousand. We need a plan that fits our actual budgets.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, B sounds fair, but moving it means new paperwork every time. I’m worried we’ll just be arguing about whose turn it is to move the bins.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, the paperwork is real, but I need to know the time cost. Does rotating mean I’m supervising twenty mornings a year?","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, the complaint log proves the current setup is unjust. One household bears the burden while the others ignore it. We need a solution that distributes the cost and responsibility equally.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@May, no, you don't have to supervise! Just move the bins. It’s easy! I promise it won’t stink as bad as the box.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@May, I agree. Rotating avoids the huge construction cost, but we must ensure the setup fees are manageable for all five of us.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, no supervision, just moving. But the clerk said each site change needs its own notice. That’s five separate filings. I’m worried we’ll be arguing over the paperwork, not the bins.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, five filings is a nightmare. But if it’s just moving, not supervising, I can live with it. I’m leaning B.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@May, rotating is the only option that physically distributes the burden. The measurements prove one frontage cannot bear it alone. I support B.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Rin,,"@Shunichi, five filings sounds scary, but I promise I’ll help! I just want the stink to move away from my nose.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Midori,,"@Shunichi, I hear your worry about the paperwork. But if we split the small setup costs, it’s manageable. I’m leaning B too.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, five filings is a hassle, but it’s better than waking up at dawn to police a window. I’m leaning B, provided we don’t let the paperwork eat us alive.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, I’m in. Ten hours of supervision is a hard no, but five filings is just admin. I’m voting B.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, the rotation is the only option that corrects the historical imbalance. I am voting B.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Rin,,"@Everyone, I vote for B! Moving it means no one gets stuck with the stink forever. I don't want a smelly box!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Midori,,"@Everyone, I am voting for B. It avoids the high construction costs and the impossible early mornings. It feels like the most balanced choice for our budgets.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, I’m voting B. It’s messy, but it’s the only one that doesn’t force us to wake up at dawn or build a stinky box.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,May,,"@Everyone, I’m voting B. Five filings is annoying, but it’s just admin. I won’t trade my mornings for a stinky box.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Everyone, I am voting B. The rotation is the only option that corrects the historical imbalance. I refuse to sign an agreement that ignores the reality of our frontages.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
